# @olie/ui

Shared library (Vue 3 JS, Vite 4) consumed by `management` and `cockpit`. Changes here break consumers silently. Details: `packages/ui/CLAUDE.md`.

## Quick architecture

- Plugin `app.use(ui)` auto-registers **all** `.vue` files via `import.meta.glob` — global name = file name
- Consumers import raw source: `@olie/ui/src/...` (`yarn build` / `dist/` is decorative)
- Services = functions (not classes); they use `api from '@utils/api'` from the **consumer** (runtime alias)
- Vuex `system` store and directives (`PermissionDirective`, `CockpitAccessDirective`) do **not** come from the plugin — manual registration in the consumer
- Helpers depend on `window.store` and `window.axios` set by the consumer
- `CheckRequestResponse` returns `false` on error — **does not throw**

## Conventions

- SFC Options API + `defineComponent()` (this package; do not mass-migrate to `<script setup>` unless asked)
- Props via JSDoc; services as exported functions; mutations UPPERCASE; utils PascalCase (`GetTagStyle`)
- Constants SCREAMING_SNAKE with labels as i18n keys
- Types in `src/types/*.ts` are IDE/reference only — **not** compiled or type-checked in the build

## Pitfalls

- Renaming `Foo.vue` renames the global component in every app
- Pin `"@olie/ui": "1.0.0"` in consumers; bump in the same PR
- Bootstrap 5 is a dep of the lib and the apps — versions must match; CSS is not auto-imported
- Coordinate `api.call()` signature changes between management and cockpit
- No exported global SCSS — each app brings its own theme
